      "problem": "Find ${f}^{′}(x)$ for $f(x)=4\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-5{x}^{2}+8.$",
      "worked_solution": "We know that $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.$ Applying this formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(4\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-5{x}^{2}+8) \\\\  & =-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-5\\cdot 2x+0 \\\\  & =-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-10x.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
